# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Property Management System ET — example environment file.
# Copy to .env and fill in real values. NEVER commit .env.
#
# Structure:
#   1. REQUIRED  — 4 lines; the API refuses to boot without the first three.
#   2. PAYMENTS  — the one switch you actually flip (Chapa / mock / Telebirr).
#   3. DEFAULTS  — everything below is commented out because the code already
#                  ships these exact values. Uncomment only to deviate.
# Read order: apps/api/.env overrides the root .env; real environment
# variables win over both. Restart the API after editing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ===========================================================================
# 1. REQUIRED
# ===========================================================================

# Local docker-compose Postgres (see docker-compose.yml)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://pms:pms@localhost:5432/pms_dev?schema=public
# Used by the test suite (integration tests truncate this database; never
# point it at the dev database). docker-compose creates pms_test for you.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://pms:pms@localhost:5432/pms_test?schema=public

# Min 32 chars. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 48
JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=change-me-development-only-access-secret-32chars

# AES-256-GCM key for fields encrypted at rest (tenant ID numbers).
# Min 32 chars. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
FIELD_ENCRYPTION_KEY=change-me-development-only-field-encryption-key

# ===========================================================================
# 2. PAYMENTS — the switch you actually flip
# ===========================================================================
# mock | telebirr | chapa
# - mock: the demo gateway, simulated end to end. Default; zero setup.
# - chapa: three modes, controlled entirely by CHAPA_SECRET_KEY:
#     1. Empty key + PAYMENT_PROVIDER=chapa  → built-in in-process sandbox
#        simulation (no real network, no Chapa account). Good for early dev.
#     2. Test key (CHASECK_TEST-...)         → real HTTP calls to
#        api.chapa.co; tenants see the real Chapa hosted checkout page,
#        pay with Chapa's published test cards / test mobile numbers
#        (developer.chapa.co/test/testing-cards and developer.chapa.co/test/
#        testing-mobile). No money
#        moves. Use this to validate the full UX on a real phone.
#     3. Live key (CHASECK-...)              → real money moves. Run in
#        production only, after compliance is approved in the Chapa dashboard.
# Toggle test↔live in the Chapa dashboard: bottom-left switch. Both modes use
# the same api.chapa.co endpoint; the key prefix decides which mode Chapa
# applies to the request. Only the SECRET key is used by this app — the
# Chapa dashboard also shows a public key (client-side widgets only) and an
# encryption key (webhook payloads); neither is needed here.
#
# Key formats in the wild (checked 2026-11-02): classic accounts issue
# CHASECK_TEST-… test keys; newer dashboards issue CHAPA_TEST_… (and label it
# "Private Key"). The two formats speak different API surfaces and the adapter
# picks automatically from the prefix: CHASECK-… → v1 (api.chapa.co/v1),
# CHAPA_TEST_… → v2 (api.chapa.global/v2, integer-cents amounts). No config
# needed — a "Callback URL must start with https://" error with a valid key
# means non-https URLs were sent (see return_url note further down), and any
# other Chapa rejection surfaces verbatim as the checkout error.
#
# What a tenant can actually pay WITH on a test key (checked 2026-11-05,
# developer.chapa.co/test/testing-mobile): only Chapa's published test
# instruments succeed — telebirr/CBEBirr/COOPPay/awash/amole numbers
# 0900123456, 0900112233, 0900881111 (Awash Bank and Amole then ask for an
# OTP: enter 12345), M-Pesa numbers 0700123456 / 0700112233 / 0700881111, and
# cards 4200 0000 0000 0000 (Visa) / 5400 0000 0000 0000 (Mastercard) with
# CVV 1234 + expiry 12/34 (other cards: CVV 123). ANY other number/wallet
# fails — or hangs at the "OTP is on its way" popup, which is what Chapa's
# test mode shows for the OTP channels when the number is not one of theirs.
# That is sandbox behavior, not a bug in this app; with a live key the real
# OTP screens appear.
#
# Return trip: Chapa only redirects the payer back to an https return_url, so
# on a http localhost checkout the receipt page has no way home. The portal
# handles this itself — "Pay now" opens the checkout in a new tab and the
# portal page watches the attempt, confirming and updating the balance on its
# own. In production (https PORTAL_RETURN_ORIGIN / CORS_ORIGINS) the redirect
# works end to end.
#
# IMPORTANT — the key is the real switch: a non-empty CHAPA_SECRET_KEY below
# runs real Chapa even if PAYMENT_PROVIDER still says mock (the default that
# ships in this file). Leave the key empty to keep the demo gateway. Also note
# an organization's own saved gateway (Organization → Payment gateway) takes
# precedence over this file, except a saved *demo* row, which real credentials
# here outrank.
PAYMENT_PROVIDER=mock
CHAPA_SECRET_KEY=

# When you wire Chapa webhooks: the webhook secret from the Chapa dashboard.
#CHAPA_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Override only for tests or inspecting proxies. Empty = the documented
# default for the key format: api.chapa.co/v1 (classic CHASECK_TEST-… keys) or
# api.chapa.global/v2 (newer CHAPA_TEST_… "Private Key" keys) — the adapter
# picks the API surface from the key prefix automatically.
#CHAPA_BASE_URL=

# Telebirr is a scaffold: even with all five values set, the provider refuses
# to run until the official Telebirr integration guide is implemented
# (ProviderNotConfiguredError). Leave everything commented until then.
#TELEBIRR_APP_ID=
#TELEBIRR_APP_KEY=
#TELEBIRR_PUBLIC_KEY=
#TELEBIRR_PRIVATE_KEY=
#TELEBIRR_SHORT_CODE=

# ===========================================================================
# 3. DEFAULTS — working values baked into the code; uncomment to deviate
# ===========================================================================

# --- API server ----------------------------------------------------------
#NODE_ENV=development
# fatal|error|warn|info|debug|trace (default: info)
#LOG_LEVEL=info
# API_PORT also honours the container-standard PORT when API_PORT is unset.
#API_PORT=4000
#API_HOST=0.0.0.0
# Comma-separated list of allowed browser origins for CORS.
#CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
# Public base URL of the API — used to build provider webhook URLs. Set it in
# production (e.g. https://api.pms.example.com) so Chapa can call back.
# MUST be an https:// URL when live Chapa is active: Chapa rejects http
# callback URLs outright ("Callback URL must start with https://"). With no
# usable callback URL the payment still completes — the portal re-verifies on
# return or when the tenant taps "check payment status".
#API_PUBLIC_URL=
# Explicit origin providers send the payer back to after a portal checkout.
# Defaults to the first CORS origin; set it when the public URL differs
# (proxies, custom domains, separate portal host). MUST be https:// when live
# Chapa is active — Chapa rejects http return URLs the same way, so in
# development (localhost) the tenant completes the payment from the portal's
# "check payment status" affordance instead of an automatic redirect.
#PORTAL_RETURN_ORIGIN=
# The origin emails link back to (accept-invite links). Defaults to the first
# CORS origin, which is the web app in every normal deployment; set it when
# the web app lives on a different host than the first CORS entry.
#WEB_APP_ORIGIN=
# These emails become platform admins at signup (no extra verification; first
# registration with the address wins). They can act inside any organization
# via the x-organization-id header. Comma separated.
#PLATFORM_ADMIN_EMAILS=

# --- Auth lifetimes -------------------------------------------------------
# The WEB session cookies below must move together with these two.
#JWT_ACCESS_TTL_SECONDS=900
#JWT_REFRESH_TTL_SECONDS=2592000

# --- Background jobs (pg-boss) -------------------------------------------
#JOBS_ENABLED=true
#WORKER_CRON_CHARGE_GENERATION=0 2 * * *
#WORKER_CRON_OVERDUE_SWEEP=30 2 * * *

# --- Auth rate limiting ---------------------------------------------------
#RATE_LIMIT_AUTH_WINDOW_MS=900000
#RATE_LIMIT_AUTH_MAX=20

# --- Whole-API rate limiting (ops hardening) ------------------------------
# Generous per-IP budget over every /api/v1 route; sheds abusive traffic and
# runaway clients without shaping normal office usage. Health checks exempt.
#RATE_LIMIT_API_WINDOW_MS=60000
#RATE_LIMIT_API_MAX=600

# --- Email / SMS notifications -------------------------------------------
# mock | resend  (Resend free tier: 3,000 emails/month, 100/day — resend.com)
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend turns on real mail for everything: signup verification
# codes, invite links, password-reset codes and tenant notifications.
# With the shared onboarding@resend.dev sender, mail only reaches the Resend
# account owner's own inbox; verify a domain and set EMAIL_FROM to reach tenants.
#EMAIL_PROVIDER=mock
#RESEND_API_KEY=
#EMAIL_FROM=Property Management <onboarding@resend.dev>
# mock | ethio-telecom-sms
#SMS_PROVIDER=mock
#SMS_API_URL=
#SMS_API_KEY=
#SMS_SENDER_NAME=

# --- File storage ---------------------------------------------------------
# Only 'local' is implemented (ADR-0006 records the S3 decision; the driver is
# a placeholder, so there are no S3 env vars yet).
#STORAGE_DRIVER=local
#STORAGE_LOCAL_DIR=./storage
#MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=10485760

# --- Web app (apps/web) ---------------------------------------------------
# The browser calls the API through the Next.js server (relative /api/v1 URLs).
# This is where that server-side proxy points. Never exposed to the browser.
#API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:4000
# Port the web dev server listens on. `pnpm dev:all` starts the API, the worker
# and the web app together; on Cloud Shell, open Web Preview for this port.
#WEB_PORT=3000
# Extra origin accepted for state-changing requests, when the proxy in front of
# the app forwards a host the app cannot guess. Normally unnecessary: the app
# accepts its own Host / x-forwarded-host. Comma-separated, full origins.
# Example: APP_ORIGIN=https://pms.example.com
#APP_ORIGIN=
# Session cookie lifetimes, in seconds — keep in sync with the JWT TTLs above.
#SESSION_ACCESS_MAX_AGE_SECONDS=900
#SESSION_REFRESH_MAX_AGE_SECONDS=2592000
# Force the Secure flag on session cookies: true | false | unset.
# Unset means "decide from x-forwarded-proto", which is what you want behind a
# TLS-terminating proxy (Cloud Shell Web Preview) *and* on plain-http localhost.
#COOKIE_SECURE=

# --- Dev process sizing (pnpm dev:all) ------------------------------------
# Per-process V8 heap caps for small machines; dev-all.mjs picks sane values
# from total RAM when unset (docs/LOCAL_DEV.md → troubleshooting).
#API_HEAP_MB=512
#WEB_HEAP_MB=2048
#WORKER_HEAP_MB=384
